  "last_message": "Pickup reminders now go by email instead of SMS. I changed `CHANNEL` from `\"sms\"` to `\"email\"` in `larder/reminders.py`, and `remind()` already sends to `member_email` when the channel isn't SMS.\n\nI also added a short page, `docs/features/reminders.md`, linked from `docs/features/README.md`. Nothing in `docs/` covered reminders before. The page says reminders go by email because SMS cost the pantry 40 euros a month, since the code alone doesn't show that reason.\n\nThe two existing tests pass, but none of them cover reminders, so this change hasn't been tested. Nothing is committed yet.\n\nTwo things I couldn't check from the repository:\n- **Email addresses:** whether every member has a working email address on file. Anyone who only has a phone number won't get the reminder any more.\n- **SMS billing:** whether the 40 euro charge stops on its own once no texts are sent, or the SMS plan also needs cancelling with the provider.",
